  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>With weak field ligands Mn(II) will be of high spin and with strong field ligands it will be of low spin. Ni(II) tetrahedral complexes will be genrally of high spin due to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation. It can very rarely be of low spin when ligand field is very strong.</p><p>Mn(II) is of light pink color in aqueous solution.</p>",
